      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How much does a garden makeover cost?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A garden tidy-up in Cornwall typically costs from \u00a380 for a half-day job. Larger makeovers including landscaping, gravel installation, and planting range from \u00a31,500 to \u00a32,500 over 2 to 3 days. Final pricing depends on garden size, current condition, and access. Send a few photos for an accurate quote within 24 hours."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How much does lawn mowing cost?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A small front lawn typically costs \u00a320 to \u00a330 per cut. An average-sized garden is around \u00a330 to \u00a350. In Cornwall\u2019s mild coastal climate, lawns grow almost year-round, so most customers book fortnightly cuts from March to October, dropping to monthly over winter. I include edging and a clean finish as standard."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long will the work take?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "A regular lawn mow or garden tidy takes 1 to 3 hours depending on size. Hedge trimming is usually half a day. Full landscaping projects like gravel gardens take 2 to 3 days. I\u2019ll confirm the exact timeline when I quote, and I always aim to complete on schedule."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can you work with my existing garden features?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, absolutely. If something can be kept or improved I\u2019ll tell you, there\u2019s no unnecessary rip-out. Many of my projects involve reshaping existing beds, working around established plants, or repositioning features to create a better layout. I\u2019ll walk you through what makes sense to keep."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do you offer ongoing maintenance?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. I offer weekly, fortnightly, and monthly maintenance visits starting from around \u00a360 per visit depending on garden size. Most of my regular clients started with a one-off tidy and liked the result enough to book ongoing care. I\u2019ll recommend a schedule that suits your garden and budget."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What areas do you cover?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "I\u2019m based in Trevarrian near Newquay and cover most of Cornwall including Truro, St Austell, Bodmin, Padstow, Perranporth, and St Ives. If you\u2019re unsure whether I reach your area, just ask. I\u2019m usually happy to travel across Cornwall for the right job."
          }
        }
